      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Administration of Islamic Law (Federal Territories) (Amendment) Bill 1995"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_1",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act may be cited as the Administration of Islamic Law (Federal Territories) (Amendment) Act 1995."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_2",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Administration of Islamic Law (Federal Territories)"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Act 1993, which in this Act is referred to as the \"principal Act\", is amended by inserting after section 8 the following \"Power to 8A. (1) The Majlis may, with the approval of establish the Yang di-Pertuan Agong, establish companies companies and under the Companies Act 1965 to carry out any validation activity which has been planned or undertaken of com- panies by the Majlis in execution of its duty or powers established. under section 7. Act 125. (2) Every company established or purported to be established by the Majlis under the Companies Act 1965 before the commencement of this section shall be deemed to have been lawfully established and shall continue to exist as if it had been established by the Majlis under subsection (1). (3) Any financing or financial assistance given by the Majlis under subsection (2) of section 7 to a company referred to in subsection (2) shall be deemed to have been lawfully given.\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "3",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3__para_b"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 58 (2) of the principal Act is amended—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for the word \"and\" a comma; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_3",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after the word \"conduct\" the words \"or discontinue\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_4",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "4",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by substituting for section"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "59 the following section: 59. (1) Subject to subsection (2), the Majlis may admit any person having sufficient knowledge of Islamic Law to be Peguam Syarie to represent parties in any proceedings before the Syariah Court. (2) The Majlis may, with the approval of the Yang di-Pertuan Agong, make rules— (a) to prcvide for the procedure, qualifications and fees for the admission of Peguam Syarie; and (b) to regulate, control and supervise the conduct of Peguam Syarie. (3) Notwithstanding subsection(l), the Majlis may exempt any member of the Judicial and Legal Service of the Federation or any person appointed under section 3 of the Legal Aid Act 1971 from the provisions of this section. (4) Notwithstanding anything contained in any other written law, no person other than a Peguam Syarie or a person exempted under subsection (3), shall be entitled to appear in any Syariah Court on behalf of any party to any proceedings before it.\". (FEDERAL TERRITORIES) (AMENDMENT)"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@/~cl_5",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "5",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/3/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 102 (2) of the principal Act is amended by"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "substituting for the figure \"95\" the figure \"96\"."
      }
    }
  ]
